An interactive physical beehive built for Aula Apícola Sierra de Hoyo de Manzanares, a beekeeping education and conservation center near Madrid. Opening the beehive starts a sound; removing a panel changes the sound depending on whether it's the queen bee or worker bee zone; closing it returns to silence.

This was build using a co-design technique with the apiary. They needed to create an storytelling educational experience to teach kids about bees without endangering them.

Built with [Naun](https://www.naun.xyz/).

**Note** : This product was a part of the "PROOFin10" service where we work with clients to transform their ideas (..or claude chats) into actual physical products in 3 weeks with €10k of client investment. The final outputs are website, physical prototype, and pitch deck.

More information : [Aula Apícola Sierra de Hoyo](https://www.aulaapicolahoyo.com/)
